# Licence files must stay byte-canonical so they remain hash-verifiable.
#
# The portfolio rule is that LICENSE-APACHE is verbatim canonical BECAUSE a
# verbatim file can be checked against the canonical text and an edited one
# cannot. That check is a sha256, and a sha256 is not line-ending agnostic.
#
# Ours hash correctly today only because this clone happens to be LF. On a
# machine with core.autocrlf=true a fresh clone would rewrite them to CRLF and
# the hash would stop matching — canonical by luck rather than by pin. Fuel's
# were CRLF and non-canonical by one leading blank line, and were cleared TWICE
# by two agents running two different narrow tests.
LICENSE-*   text eol=lf
